# OpenTTD needs these to play music.
# <twb> I want https://tracker.debian.org/pkg/timidity in D14;
#       it's currently blocked by #1039396 which has
#       Ubuntu patches at the bottom that I think we should just take.
#       Debian#1039396: timidity: ships sysv-init script without systemd unit - https://bugs.debian.org/1039396
# <twb> My actual end goal is working music in openttd
# <twb> Looks like fluidsynth might work as a replacement for openttd specifically
# <twb> OK so FTR: openttd can play music as long as you have libfluidsynth
#       (pulled in by normal hard Depends) and fluid-soundfont-gs and/or fluid-soundfont-gm, and
#       also it needs an actual .mid file
#       which it normally downloads from bananas-cdn.openttd.org per-user.
#       It DOES NOT need /bin/timidity nor /bin/fluidsynth.
# <twb> I initially mis-diagnosed just because
#       the various mixers were all set low enough
#       I couldn't hear the music over the cooling fan.
# NOT NEEDED: timidity,
 fluid-soundfont-gm,
Conflicts:
